 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "### Plotting Kaplan-Meir curves",
   "segment_index": "S11.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:315-315",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.ru.qmd:315-315",
   "proposition": "The English says the plotted curve illustrates the survival experience in the whole patient group (one group); the Russian says it illustrates the survival experience in two whole groups of patients ('в двух полных группах пациентов').",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader believes the plot beside this text shows two stratified curves, when the fitted object is linelistsurv_fit from survfit(survobj ~ 1), a single marginal curve for the entire cohort. They then misread the single step curve and may look for a group comparison that only appears many sections later.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Fitting a Cox model",
   "segment_index": "S15.P5",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:572-572",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.ru.qmd:572-572",
   "proposition": "The English attributes the negative association with all-cause mortality to the onset-to-admission duration (the days_onset_hosp covariate); the Russian attributes it twice to 'продолжительность госпитализации', the duration of the hospital stay.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader concludes that a longer hospital stay reduces the risk of death by 10.7% per day, an entirely different and unsupported claim. The covariate in the fitted model at line 554 is days_onset_hosp, days from symptom onset to admission, and the Russian text at line 546 defines it correctly, so the reader also gets two contradictory definitions of the same variable within one section.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Data management and transformation",
   "segment_index": "S6.P5",
   "kind": "missing",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:169-169",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.ru.qmd:169-169",
   "proposition": "The English carries a cross-reference link to the Descriptive tables page, [Descriptive tables](tables_descriptive.qmd); the Russian keeps only the bracketed label [Описательные таблицы] with no link target.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader sees literal square brackets rather than a link and cannot navigate to the Descriptive tables page for the tabyl() and adorn_* explanation that this sentence explicitly defers to.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "## Time-dependent covariates in survival models",
   "segment_index": "S17.P1",
   "kind": "added",
   "en_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.qmd:615-615",
   "tr_span": "chapters/survival_analysis.ru.qmd:615-615",
   "proposition": "The Russian calls the adapted source a book ('превосходной книги'); the English describes it only as an introduction to survival analysis in R, which is a web tutorial.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader may search for a published book by Emily Zabor rather than following the linked online tutorial.",
